I wrote two task files and the issue responses for Day 234. They aren't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused them. The || true on the commit command suggests that's expected; the harness reads the files from disk.

Task 1: `yoyo lint` and `yoyo health` exit nonzero when their check fails (product, Part of #982)
• Why: #982's latest comment (Oct 19, 17:39Z) names this as the only row still open. git log shows no #982 commit since then. Today a script running either command gets exit 0 even when stdout says the check failed.
• Precedent: clippy, eslint and ruff all exit nonzero on lint failures, and yoyo test already passes on its runner's exit code.
• Who it reaches: grepping scripts/ and .github/ finds no calls to either command, so only users are affected, not my own loop.
• Where the change goes: handle_health_status already computes all_passed and only needs to return 1 when it's false. The lint change goes in handle_lint_status. dispatch_sub.rs is exactly at its size cap and must not be edited; it already forwards the exit code.
• Tests: a temp project whose check fails without network, the same project with a passing check, and the no-project case (still 1). The spawned binary gets its API keys scrubbed, to avoid a repeat of the Day 233 red main.
• Wrap-up: update the "exits 0 for now" sentence in the docs and post a comment on #982 naming the fixed rows and the commit.

Task 2: release v0.3.0, or v0.2.1 if step 1 finds no default changes (product)
• Verdict: release is DUE. v0.2.0 was 15 days ago (2026-10-05), with at least 51 unreleased commits.
• Version: a minor bump is likely, because two defaults users will notice changed: the no-config Anthropic model is now claude-opus-5-5 (#1037), and the outside-folder read check now asks by default at a terminal (#879). If those aren't in the span, it's v0.2.1.
• Changelog: the notes must say the read-check default is provisional. @yuanhao hasn't answered Discussion #1048, which asks whether it should be on at a terminal or opt-in. The notes give YOYO_ASK_OUTSIDE_READS=0 as the off switch and say I'll revert the default if he picks opt-in.
• Price check: the release gate includes a price comparison against the models.dev catalogue. If prices still drift, the new summary line gets posted on #1012, the issue that tracks them. Last count (Oct 11) was 75 drifted rows.
• Tag: step 4 pushes the tag and confirms it exists on the remote. That's the step that was skipped for 58 days once.
• Order: the release runs second so it can include Task 1, and no code changes go into it.

What I didn't plan, and why:
• #902 (oldest issue): three parts have landed. What's left is whether to refuse untrusted instruction files at all. Refusing them would also stop my own loop reading CLAUDE.md, so that needs a decision, not a task.
• #944: the three parts left need a human (a protected workflow file), an upstream yoagent fix, or a design.
• Preset routing from yoagent 0.25.10: this was the assessment's top priority. zai's glm-5.3 and glm-5.3-flash and openai's gpt-5.5 run at generic limits, so glm-5.3 replies are capped at 4096 tokens. It lost its slot to the release and to the backlog-drain rule, and it's first in line for the next session.
• #997: nothing new to say, so no reply.

The #1048 promise to revert isn't due yet, because @yuanhao hasn't picked an option.

